{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789309613,"nonce":"bh8nNneERgRUu3CLHLHpErw7Fqk=","title":"An LLVM OSR entry is refused when a cold callee is still interpreted, so a hot loop never reaches the top tier","message":"bench_free_call and bench_inlined_call: the loop in main calls nothing\n(AIR inlined `step`), so `wants_callees` is false and the OSR module\ncompiles no callees; the `println` after the loop leaves `Fun_20` and\n`Fun_24` as declarations, and `bind_module_declarations` refuses a\nbytecode declaration with no installed address:\n\n    [osr] LLVM AIR entry declined findex=23 pc=6: osr module osr_23_6 has 2 unresolved symbol(s): Fun_20, Fun_24\n    [tier] findex=23 own-module refused (promote module promote_23 has 2 unresolved symbol(s): Fun_20, Fun_24); retrying through the shared module\n\nConsequences, measured on the NUC (release, HEAD 32415d0):\n- `--mode hybrid` (default): the loop runs to completion in the Cranelift\n  OSR entry. ASH_PROFILE=sample: 92-93% of samples in `Fun_23 [cranelift]`,\n  0 in llvm. free_call 90ms / inlined_call 99ms against ash-aot 70ms.\n- `--jit-tier llvm`: nothing can take the frame, so the loop is\n  INTERPRETED to the end: free_call 5.7s.\n- CI (bench page, 4-core runners): hybrid 159/159ms on free/inlined where\n  the JVM is 142/148 and ash-aot 97/98.\n\nThe same refusal is why the own-module promote path falls back to the\nshared module for any function with a cold uncompiled callee (24738d7).\n\nFix: give every bytecode callee the module declares, does not define, and\nno tier has installed a private body that calls through its\n`functions_ptrs` slot, stub-guarded like the lazy path's indirect call\n(`define_table_trampolines`, called from the OSR build and from\n`promote_in_own_module`). The trampoline leaves `func_cache` once built:\n`default\u003cO2\u003e` inlines and deletes it, and a value still held in that map\ndangled into `LLVMCountBasicBlocks` (a sig=11 at fault_addr 0x8 recovered\nas \"native fault during promotion\" in `--jit-tier llvm`).\n\nWith the entry building, the re-tier poll rule in\n`cranelift/air.rs::retier_worth_polling` was the next gate: it polled only\nloops containing a call, on a measurement taken while this refusal made\nthe hand-off impossible for call-free loops, so the poll could only cost.\nCall-free un-nested leaf loops now poll too (`ASH_RETIER_POLL_CALLS_ONLY=1`\nrestores the old rule).","files":null}]}